      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the black ink dot from last time, sitting on a pencil line near the bottom of a paper strip. Stand the strip in a jar with a little water, below the line, and put on the lid. The water slowly soaks up the paper, and as it passes the ink, the black dot comes apart. A blue dye, a pink dye and a yellow dye end up at three different heights. They all started on the same line, and they all had the same time. So why do mixture components travel different distances in chromatography?",
