      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Chromatography always has two parts. The paper is the stationary phase, the part that stays still. The water is the mobile phase, the part that moves. It climbs the paper the way a spill soaks into a paper towel, drawn up into the tiny gaps between the paper's fibres. As it climbs, it carries the dissolved dyes with it, but not all at the same speed.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
