      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Two classic traps. Measure from the baseline, not from the bottom edge of the paper, and to the centre of each spot. And put the spot's distance on top. If you ever get an R F bigger than one, you've flipped it. Here's a way to remember the whole idea. Spot over front, and stickier stays lower. The spot cannot pass the front. And the dye that sticks to the paper most has the smallest R F.",
